    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0568" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">368.117/138</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 285</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    concerning the impressment of American citizens into the Greek Army there is
                    enclosed a <pb facs="0569" n="455" xml:id="pg455"/> copy of despatch No. 249 of
                    June 1, 1922, from the United States High Commissioner at Constantinople. You
                    are instructed to take this matter up with the Foreign Office making urgent
                    representations that appropriate instructions be sent by the Greek Minister of
                    War to the local Greek military commanders in Asia Minor that they cease
                    impressing American citizens of Ottoman or Greek origin into the Greek
                        Army.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d377-f1"/></p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A.
                            Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d377-f1" n="33" xml:id="d377-f1-content">
                <p>With this instruction the correspondence in regard to the impressment of American
                    naturalized citizens into the Greek Army was temporarily discontinued.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
